# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever happens to clone the repository.
#
# Two separate things were wrong before this file existed:
#
#   - `server/src/main.cpp` was committed with CRLF while every other source file was LF. Nothing
#     noticed because a C++ compiler does not care, but it makes the repository inconsistent with
#     itself and a text patch written against one form silently misses the other.
#   - `docker/run-parity.sh` reached the Linux container with CRLF, so bash read `set -euo pipefail\r`
#     and reported "pipefail: invalid option name" on line 2. The local Linux gate had been dying
#     there, and exiting 0 while it did.
#
# `text=auto` makes git store LF for everything it detects as text and hand out the platform's own
# form on checkout, which is what `core.autocrlf` on Windows already expects. Nothing tracked here
# is binary today; if that changes, add an explicit `-text` line for it rather than loosening this.
* text=auto

# A shell script is read by a shell, not by the platform, and that shell is bash inside a Linux
# container regardless of who checked the file out.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
